# Rakumux release signing keys: minisign (Ed25519) public keys, one per line,
# each the second line of a `minisign -G` public key file (`RW...`, 56
# characters), optionally followed by a name. `#` starts a comment.
#
# Installed Rakumux (the updater, `U` and automatic updates: built in from this
# file by tui/src/updater/signature.rs), https://rakumux.com/install.sh (a copy,
# written by `release-scripts/release-keys.sh sync`) and publish-npm.sh accept a
# release only when its checksums.txt.minisig is a signature by one of these
# keys. `main`'s secret is kept offline; a key named `ci` is the one the release
# workflow signs with, a secret of its protected `release` environment.
#
# A key added here reaches installed copies with the next release they verify,
# signed by a key they already trust; see "Rotation" in install/AGENTS.md. Add
# one as:
# RWQ...its 56 characters... ci
RWSbAhedaBF6C8DldJ7V1E44o4xiwGcF5k8uNDRmH0+k4drHtANpaq2E main
